{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1530344-mau-2e-curious-cats-of-mau-backerkit","id":1530344,"title":"Mau 2E = Curious Cats of Mau BackerKit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Partner Worlds","Realms of Pugmire"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-08T23:03:17-08:00","id":1530344,"title":"Mau 2E = Curious Cats of Mau BackerKit","content":"Second Edition of <b>Monarchies of Mau</b> is coming! On Tuesday 20th of February is start of BackerKit of it. Here is link to crowdfunding page!<br /> <br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://d1wgd08o7gfznj.cloudfront.net/uploads/email_campaign/hero_image/29723/optimized_Curious_Cats_Video_Splash_Coming_Soon.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://d1wgd08o7gfznj.cloudfront.net/uploads/email_campaign/hero_image/29723/optimized_Curious_Cats_Video_Splash_Coming_Soon.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://d1wgd08o7gfznj.cloudfront.net/uploads/email_campaign/hero_image/29723/optimized_Curious_Cats_Video_Splash_Coming_Soon.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.backerkit.com/call_to_action/d9e2aef4-a45e-4ecd-8247-9936f5d956a1/landing?preview_mode=true\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.backerkit.com/call_to_ac...view_mode=true</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T03:28:31-08:00","id":1530628,"title":"","content":"It must be time for a new Pugmire book, because I get to correct Wyrdhamster again! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's not a second edition of Monarchies of Mau. While a lot of the material from Monarchies of Mau will be updated to the new edition, it's no longer a standalone game so it's not a &quot;new edition&quot; in that sense. However, this means we now have room for a lot of new material that wasn't ever in the original books, so come check it out!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-20T11:58:24-08:00","id":1531204,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.backerkit.com/c/projects/onyx-path/curious-cats-of-mau\" target=\"_blank\"><b>And it's MEOW... a LIVE!!!</b></a><br /> <br /> Here is cover graphic<br /> <br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://bk-prod.imgix.net/active_storage/backerkit_production/blob/if9dnm297cftg2j8vupkyvzbdm2i?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;auto=compress%2C%20format&amp;cs=srgb&amp;q=80&amp;fit=max&amp;w=1360&amp;lossless=true\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://bk-prod.imgix.net/active_storage/backerkit_production/blob/if9dnm297cftg2j8vupkyvzbdm2i?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;auto=compress%2C%20format&amp;cs=srgb&amp;q=80&amp;fit=max&amp;w=1360&amp;lossless=true\" data-thumb-url=\"https://bk-prod.imgix.net/active_storage/backerkit_production/blob/if9dnm297cftg2j8vupkyvzbdm2i?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;auto=compress%2C%20format&amp;cs=srgb&amp;q=80&amp;fit=max&amp;w=1360&amp;lossless=true\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The BackerKit crowdfunding lasts for a month, until March 21st, and chapters of the later beta manual for supporters will be made available every week.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">\u2022 We play as humanoid cats in 6 (7?) fantastical Monarchies, experiencing adventures and intrigues like in a more family friendly version of 'Game of Thrones'. <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83d\ude40</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">\u2022 The Realms of Pugmire line \u2013 of which #CuriousCats is now a part \u2013 uses the Onyx20 mechanic \u2013 which started out as a more narrative variant of the 5E D&amp;D system. Now it departs further from the classic d20 assumptions, such as by limiting to only 10 levels, characters receive the equivalent of Feats with each level - and the party uses a large pool of the Fortune meta currency during the game.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">\u2022 In 2E, character creation based on templates is added. Compared to fully creating a character from all materials (which is still an option), according to a template we choose a few features from the presented options or even roll them randomly.<span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83c\udfb2</span> Tests show that creating using templates takes up to 10 minutes per character! <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83d\ude3a</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">\u2022 The enemy <b>Morale</b> mechanic is also new - enemies are generally stronger than in 1E, but we now have mechanical support to force them to escape or intimidate them not to attack. <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83d\ude3c</span> There are even rules on how to make new friends! <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83d\ude3b</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">\u2022 Curious Cats of Mau is an SUPPLEMENT to the Realms of Pugmire 2E core game from last year. Which means that in Curious Cats they don't have to deal with repeating mechanics, and Mau 2E means new materials or options (mainly) for Cats! <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83d\ude3b</span> During crowdfunfing, you can also order the RoP 2E core about dogs at a lower price. <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83d\udc36</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">\u2022 The space for other materials has also been increased - in Curious Cats there are 8 compared to the previous 6 Callings (Character Classes) from Mau 1E, including 2 from Pirates of Pugmire - Torpedo guns shooting and Mystic witch-druids. <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83d\ude3a</span> New spells for 3 (!) Charming Callings - as well as a campaign of 3 related adventures for Cats. And a lot more!</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">\u2022 Finally, the description of the Monarchs themselves has been delved much deeper, including updates to the situation with the Ruling Council and the relations with Pugmire, the Dog Empire. There are even more intrigues for heroic cats to fight against!</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-21T05:04:26-08:00","id":1531229,"title":"","content":"So, if I read correctly, <b>Preview 1 - Introduction &amp; Report of Castellan</b> - to Mau 2E / #CuriousCats does not bring anything new except 1 or 2 inspirational positions.<br /> The only 3 world changes in the overview of Monarchies are: 1. There is the new ruler of Threnody von Mau.<br /> 2. Pugmire and Monarchies withdrew their ambassadors to each other, cooling their relations.<br /> 3. A general description of badgers, birds and reptiles is indicated in the text. (Because they were described after the release of Mau 1E.)<br /> <br /> Did I miss something in text?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T01:07:24-08:00","id":1531497,"title":"","content":"If only there were more chapters coming that would give more information.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T01:52:33-08:00","id":1531499,"title":"","content":"I was kinda hoping to splurge on one of the higher tier rewards this time around, but alas, they got snatched up mighty fast.<br /> <br /> Also, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a>, you literally cited a bunch of things that are new in the general non-manuscript preview from the pledge page. We're getting new stuff too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T00:29:08-08:00","id":1531604,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/hashtag/mau?__eep__=6&amp;__cft__%5b0%5d=AZUmG1LN0b8KWBHXH-zVKRtpcDcgTvuNVAsspupkpo-68-z0R-bz1czjwYuS-HJKXwzMiCxNe51TcCdiGfTbXzyPQgmHjb1nqOwqMOJhNmrhAtNVtixN3G30RuW-vxg_VWC7JQP6qcMsCZrjesWWb9RZwIflj8VKkc7u-ZrvkQHrblyOao3w8vEhqT0GA8H0ml0&amp;__tn__=*NK-R\" target=\"_blank\">#Mau</a> 2E / <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/hashtag/curiouscats?__eep__=6&amp;__cft__%5b0%5d=AZUmG1LN0b8KWBHXH-zVKRtpcDcgTvuNVAsspupkpo-68-z0R-bz1czjwYuS-HJKXwzMiCxNe51TcCdiGfTbXzyPQgmHjb1nqOwqMOJhNmrhAtNVtixN3G30RuW-vxg_VWC7JQP6qcMsCZrjesWWb9RZwIflj8VKkc7u-ZrvkQHrblyOao3w8vEhqT0GA8H0ml0&amp;__tn__=*NK-R\" target=\"_blank\">#CuriousCats</a> \u2013 In todays blog post Onyx Path share legend about catls Fallen Monarchy - Smilodon!</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><img title=\"dataurl519039.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1496_1709022519338_688\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1496\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1496\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1496&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"dataurl519039.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/> </span><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Smilodon\u2019s loss stings so profoundly because its cats were once some of Mau\u2019s most excellent. After all the easily-settled lands were occupied, the houses skirmished over desirable crossroads or fertile fields along their borders. And yet, thought some intrepid cats, weren\u2019t there lands yet unclaimed at the edge of broken cliffs and salt flat? Rocky beach and tangled forest?</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">These bands organized under Rasmus von Smilodon, a student of Angora\u2019s libraries and Mau\u2019s universities, a polymath who studied natural science and practical engineering. A cat of enormous ambition, he built wind traps and cisterns further into the desert than Angora had ever dared, raised mountainside gardens and vertical towns on slopes Korat had dismissed, and even drained lands thought lost to the Acid Sea. His followers were equally impressive. Cassius von Smilodon developed soaring treehouses in western forests, while Pasha von Smilodon\u2019s glass houses enabled the cultivation of plants in parts of Siberian territory that had never seen a harvest. It was no secret that von Smilodon and his followers planned to follow in Cymric\u2019s mold: offer services to the monarchies and be rewarded with lands in return.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">However, it was a different age than Cymric\u2019s founding. No house was willing to give up contiguous parcels of valuable land, even with all of Smilodon\u2019s good works. Instead, the monarchies reached a rare compromise; each would give Smilodon those lands they found difficult to cultivate \u2014 or even survive in \u2014 for surely Smilodon\u2019s followers could make better use of them? And so House Smilodon found itself spread across the breadth of Mau. The bold, clever cats wrestled unwilling lands into submission, raising chapterhouses and mansions across wasteland, mire, and blight. This chilled relations between Smilodon the other monarchies, but still the house prospered.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">House Smilodon\u2019s works became landmarks wherever they were: the Great Desert Sundial of the Northern Dunes, the Distillation Houses of the Acid Coast, the Great Glass Dome of the frigid heights. From them, intrepid explorers issued. Cartographer Cassius von Mau charted ever more paths through the Fearful Forest. Pasha von Smilodon erected the finest pleasure gardens and heated mansions across the north. Dandan von Smilodon made contact with three different species of reptiles, parlaying access to Smilodon\u2019s windtraps and water stores for regular visits by new traders.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Still, no matter how celebrated their works and discoveries became, House Smilodon became restless. Perhaps one-too-many scheming neighbors soured the rank and file, or perhaps the cats attracted to Smilodon\u2019s banner were always destined to cast their gaze over the next horizon. The house\u2019s explorers ranged further and further away, both in geographical distance and willingness to take new risks. Adventurers delivered strange devices and suspect magics to House Smilodon chapterhouses even as they shared more prosaic discoveries with all of Mau\u2019s cats.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">When explorers brought word that there were strange Old One artifacts scattered around traversable pathways through the northern mountains, Rasmus himself lead the first major expedition. At great cost of material and catpower, his expedition reached beyond the cold cliffs to find the eerie, blasted scape. From the closest foothills to the mountain\u2019s northern edge, discolored earth sprouted unnatural weeds, stretching into blighted plains. Jagged, irregular ruins were arranged like mandalas around enormous pits that fulminated choking smoke. The presence of the Unseen loomed more heavily the closer they got to the pits, but Rasmus was determined to explore these strange findings\u2026</span></i><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Reading this gave me chills all over again, and there\u2019s lots more intriguing information for you to discover. Even as I\u2019m typing this, I\u2019m thinking of a bunch of other cool things I\u2019m excited for people to read. Maybe Rich will invite me back for more tidbits next week (hint, hint), but it\u2019s time for me to wrap this blurb up. In the meantime, please check out the Backerkit campaign to learn more!</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-27-2024, 03:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T00:36:14-08:00","id":1531605,"title":"","content":"'Cartographer <b>Cassius von Mau</b> charted ever more paths through the Fearful Forest.' - Should not be <b>Cassius von Smilodon</b>, like a rest of great inventors of Smilodon mentioned in text? \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-29T15:10:39-08:00","id":1531746,"title":"","content":"I'm getting both the corebook and the cat extension. Will the rats, mice, birds, and lizards be reprinted too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T01:33:29-08:00","id":1531944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1530344-mau-2e-curious-cats-of-mau-backerkit?p=1531746#post1531746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm getting both the corebook and the cat extension. Will the rats, mice, birds, and lizards be reprinted too?</div> </div> </div> </div>In different books, but yes. There will be a rodent-specific sourcebook like Curious Cats of Mau, and birds and reptiles will be put into a different sourcebook which isn't exclusively pirate-focused. Stay tuned!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-18T22:31:08-07:00","id":1532835,"title":"","content":"FINALLY we have some sum-ups of Curious Cats of Mau 3 adventures inside book. Grab it of you can right now, BackerKit campaign for it ends in 2 days! <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monday Meeting Notes</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all the excitement about the cool updates to the material we\u2019re doing for Curious Cats of Mau, I wanted to mention that it also contains three entire adventures which comprise a loose campaign! Check these bad boys out!<br /> <br /> Eventide and Dawn<br /> After the characters halt an attempted murder, they\u2019re hired to find out who hired the assassins and why. As they unravel the mystery, they uncover a conspiracy worming its way into the heart of the monarchies. This is an introductory adventure suitable for level 1 characters.<br /> <br /> Enemy or Ally<br /> Ally von Rex has learned that the characters are more than capable of disrupting her plans and that of House Smilodon. The only way to ensure they won\u2019t meddle is to take them out. Little does she realize that by trying to deal with them preemptively, she\u2019s given them a clue to her greater scheme. Now she\u2019s trying to enact her plan before the characters catch up to her, and she\u2019s throwing everything she has in their way to destroy them before she fails in her task. \u201cEnemy or Ally\u201d is an adventure for characters at levels 3-4.<br /> <br /> Forsaken Shadows Gather<br /> When the heroes discover a plot by House Smilodon to corrupt innocent cats and infiltrate a summit where the monarchies plan to discuss how to face the resurgent Unseen threat of the fallen house, the duty to stop the worst from happening falls upon them. This is a challenging and dangerous adventure, meant for level 5-6 characters.<br /> <br /> That means that, using absolutely nothing but the book, you have enough material for an entire campaign of about five to eight sessions. With a little work to come up with missions between those (using the books suggestions of helpful story hooks), you can expand that to take the characters from level 1 to level 6 over a dozen sessions or more, and get them ready for even greater adventures at higher level. It\u2019s an entire campaign book of mystery, intrigue, and dangerous demonic adventure!</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T23:28:13-07:00","id":1533683,"title":"","content":"Except in audio of Cats telling about Secrecy in their culture to Dogs - and why there cannot be Treaty between Pugmire and May \ud83d\ude32 - Around 19:00 of <a href=\"http://I&#39;m%20listening%20to%20Onyx%20Pathcast%20%7C%20Episode%20305:%20Excerpts%20and%20Pairings%20on%20Podbean,%20check%20it%20out!%20https://www.podbean.com/ea/pb-fmi92-15d2df4\" target=\"_blank\">this Pathcast</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}